  "notes": "Band-member co-writer/producer supplying the piano-and-guitar architecture for stadium singer-songwriter pop. The drum claim is that there barely is one: \"minimal — a kick and clap or a brushed kit that enters at the second verse; on the up-tempo records a programmed kick/clap with a shaker. Percussion is a dynamic tool, not a groove.\" So the kick density is 1—2, the snare is a `soft`-transient clap, `hihat.continuous` is false at `fillDensity` 0.08 with the roll vocabulary off, and the fills are pushed to 16 bars — a dynamic tool does not repeat every four. The tresillo the Lane line names (\"frequent tresillo accenting\") is `kick.tresilloBias` 0.44, which is what keeps this model apart from the other quiet piano producers in this section. No `bass808` block: \"no 808. Electric bass or low piano octaves on roots\", which is a kick mirror at 0.90. Harmony is \"guitar and piano keys with suspended and add9 voicings and a borrowed minor iv\", so `susSubstitutionProb` is 0.48, `ninth` is raised and the `borrowed` map carries the iv; \"as a Snow Patrol guitarist/pianist his instinct is the slow-build alt-rock progression rather than a pop vamp\" is why `harmonicRhythm` has no `vamp` value and the phrases run 4 and 8 bars. The documented method is co-location rather than a sound — \"moving to Nashville and then Los Angeles to write an album, then spending a whole year on the next one … the songs are written jointly at instruments rather than to tracks\" — which is the long additive arrangement with a real bridge and endings that reduce to one instrument. ⚠ `confidence` is medium and the research says why: \"parametric detail inferred\", with its own [LOW-CONF] mark on the alt-rock progression claim repeated here. Every drum probability, the humanize numbers and `bpm.mode` 88 (the midpoint of the first-named 76—100 ballad band) are INFERRED. ⚠ **The bassline reached 892 of 1,000 distinct against `bass.rs`'s 0.95 share, and the tempo line is the citation.** The research is *\"backbeat on 2&4 straight with **frequent tresillo accenting**\"* — an accent ahead of the beat is what `anticipationProb` writes — over *\"electric bass or low piano octaves on roots\"*, which is why `followRootsProb` stays high at 0.90 and the `1 5 8` cells are untouched. ⚠ **INFERRED:** the exact 0.90 and 0.20 are lane-conventional; the entry marks its parametric detail inferred already.",
